 Integration Guide
Connect your backend to SOURCEAPI with three calls: game list → launch URL → (optional) your webhook for bet/win events. Your API key, secret, and base URL are on API Details.

Before you integrate
Copy api_key, api_secret, and base URL from API Details.
Always send vendor_code as "sourceapi" (lowercase) on every request.
Use the same member_account string every time for a given player so wallet callbacks match your users.
Know your supplier codes (e.g. CQ9, SPADE): send supplier_code on launch if your operator gave you a list per game; otherwise the platform default may apply.
All requests are POST with Content-Type: application/json unless noted.
If the operator enabled IP or domain restrictions, whitelist your server in advance.
API overview
Endpoint	Purpose
POST /api/gameList	List games (from catalog) grouped by category.
POST /api/getGameUrl	Get a one-time game launch URL for a player.
POST /api/placeBet	Same launch flow with explicit transfer_id; balance checks apply.
You do not implement the upstream wallet callback URL — SOURCEAPI does. Register https://sourceapi.com/api/callback/sourceapi only with your games operator, not in your own code.

Authentication
Send credentials on every request using one of these styles.

Option A — JSON body (recommended)
{
  "api_key": "YOUR_API_KEY",
  "api_secret": "YOUR_API_SECRET",
  ...
}
Option B — HTTP headers
X-Api-Key: YOUR_API_KEY
X-Api-Secret: YOUR_API_SECRET
You may combine headers with a JSON body that omits duplicate keys.

Two “vendor” concepts
Field	Value	Meaning
vendor_code	Always sourceapi	Tells SOURCEAPI which integration to use. Required on all client API calls.
supplier_code or provider	e.g. CQ9	Upstream game vendor code for launch. Use when your catalog or operator requires it. Either field name works.
POST /api/gameList
Returns games from the catalog. Use game_uid from the response when calling getGameUrl.

Parameters
Field	Required	Description
api_key	Yes*	Your API key.
api_secret	Yes*	Your API secret.
vendor_code	Yes	Must be sourceapi.
currency	No	Filter/context (e.g. USD, INR).
category / category_name	No	Filter by category name (exact match, case-insensitive).
search	No	Search in game names / UIDs.
limit_per_category / limit	No	Max games per category; 0 = no limit.
* Or send via X-Api-Key / X-Api-Secret headers.

Example request
POST https://sourceapi.com/api/gameList
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "api_key": "YOUR_API_KEY",
  "api_secret": "YOUR_API_SECRET",
  "vendor_code": "sourceapi",
  "currency": "INR"
}
Example success response
{
  "success": true,
  "categories": [
    {
      "name": "Slots",
      "icon": null,
      "games": [
        {
          "game_uid": "MY_GAME_001",
          "name": "Sample Slot",
          "image_url": "https://..."
        }
      ],
      "games_count": 1
    }
  ]
}
POST /api/getGameUrl
Creates a session and returns game_launch_url. Open it in a browser or WebView. member_account, game_uid, and vendor_code are required.

Parameters
Field	Required	Description
api_key / api_secret	Yes*	Credentials.
vendor_code	Yes	sourceapi.
member_account	Yes	Stable player ID in your system.
game_uid	Yes	From gameList (your public game id).
amount / credit_amount	No	Initial display / session amount (numeric). Wallet rules still apply.
currency_code	Recommended	ISO-style code (e.g. matches your account).
supplier_code or provider	Conditional	Upstream vendor when not using platform default.
language	No	e.g. en, zh.
home_url	No	Where the player returns after exiting the game.
callback_url	No	Override default upstream callback base (rare).
Example request
POST https://sourceapi.com/api/getGameUrl
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "api_key": "YOUR_API_KEY",
  "api_secret": "YOUR_API_SECRET",
  "vendor_code": "sourceapi",
  "member_account": "player_123",
  "game_uid": "MY_GAME_001",
  "amount": 100,
  "currency_code": "INR",
  "supplier_code": "CQ9",
  "language": "en",
  "home_url": "https://yoursite.com/lobby"
}
Example success response
{
  "success": true,
  "game_launch_url": "https://...",
  "data": { }
}
POST /api/placeBet
Same seamless launch path with an explicit transfer_id for idempotency in your logs. Response shape matches getGameUrl success (plus transfer_id and payload).

Extra / important parameters
Field	Required	Description
member_account	Yes	Player id.
transfer_id / transaction_id	No	Your unique id; generated if omitted.
Example request
{
  "api_key": "YOUR_API_KEY",
  "api_secret": "YOUR_API_SECRET",
  "vendor_code": "sourceapi",
  "member_account": "player_123",
  "game_uid": "MY_GAME_001",
  "amount": 100,
  "transfer_id": "shop_order_98765",
  "currency_code": "INR",
  "supplier_code": "CQ9"
}
Example success response
{
  "success": true,
  "game_launch_url": "https://...",
  "transfer_id": "shop_order_98765",
  "payload": { }
}
Copy-paste examples
cURL — game list
curl -s -X POST "https://sourceapi.com/api/gameList" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"api_key":"YOUR_KEY","api_secret":"YOUR_SECRET","vendor_code":"sourceapi","currency":"USD"}'
cURL — launch game
curl -s -X POST "https://sourceapi.com/api/getGameUrl" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"api_key":"YOUR_KEY","api_secret":"YOUR_SECRET","vendor_code":"sourceapi","member_account":"u1","game_uid":"MY_GAME_001","amount":100,"currency_code":"USD","supplier_code":"CQ9"}'
JavaScript (fetch) — launch
const res = await fetch("https://sourceapi.com/api/getGameUrl", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    api_key: "YOUR_KEY",
    api_secret: "YOUR_SECRET",
    vendor_code: "sourceapi",
    member_account: "player_123",
    game_uid: "MY_GAME_001",
    amount: 100,
    currency_code: "USD",
    supplier_code: "CQ9",
  }),
});
const data = await res.json();
if (data.success && data.game_launch_url) {
  window.location.href = data.game_launch_url;
}
Calling from the browser exposes your secret — use only for quick tests. Production: call SOURCEAPI from your server.

PHP — launch and redirect
$ch = curl_init('https://sourceapi.com/api/getGameUrl');
curl_setopt_array($ch, [
    CURLOPT_POST => true,
    CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS => json_encode([
        'api_key' => 'YOUR_API_KEY',
        'api_secret' => 'YOUR_API_SECRET',
        'vendor_code' => 'sourceapi',
        'member_account' => 'player_123',
        'game_uid' => 'MY_GAME_001',
        'amount' => 100,
        'currency_code' => 'USD',
        'supplier_code' => 'CQ9',
    ]),
    CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER => ['Content-Type: application/json'],
    CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER => true,
]);
$res = json_decode(curl_exec($ch), true);
if (!empty($res['success']) && !empty($res['game_launch_url'])) {
    header('Location: ' . $res['game_launch_url']);
    exit;
}
http_response_code(502);
echo $res['error'] ?? 'Launch failed';
Your webhook (optional)
Set your HTTPS URL under API Details. SOURCEAPI POSTs JSON when a bet, win, or cancel is processed so you can sync your own ledger.

{
  "event": "bet_win",
  "type": "bet",
  "member_account": "player_123",
  "round_id": "round_1",
  "transaction_id": "tx_abc",
  "bet_amount": 1,
  "win_amount": 0,
  "amount": 1,
  "balance_after": 99.5,
  "provider": "sourceapi",
  "currency_code": "INR",
  "timestamp": 1708416000
}
type values: bet, win, cancel. Respond with HTTP 200 quickly; failures are logged.

Errors and HTTP status
HTTP	Typical cause
200	Success.
400	Missing/invalid fields, unknown game, insufficient wallet balance for launch.
401	Missing or wrong api_key / api_secret.
402	Prepaid / GGR balance too low (see error and optional code: INSUFFICIENT_GGR_BALANCE).
403	IP/domain not allowed, or PROVIDER_NOT_ENABLED (manager accounts).
404	vendor_code not mapped or game not found.
429	Too many requests (rate limit).
500	Server or upstream error — message in error.
Error bodies are JSON, e.g. {"error":"Unknown vendor_code"}. Always check HTTP status and parse error before redirecting users to a game.

Need help?
Confirm vendor_code is exactly sourceapi, credentials match API Details, and game_uid exists in the game list response. For launch errors mentioning brand_id or upstream config, contact your platform administrator.